\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces SHAP dependence plot for distance to permanent water (Random Forest, 1{,}000 training rows). Points are individual samples coloured by NDWI; the black line and band show the decile-binned median and interquartile range of the SHAP value. The relationship is strongly non-monotonic: samples within the first distance bin (median $\approx 30$~m) receive clearly negative SHAP values, while all farther bins shift toward positive contributions.}}{16}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dependence-dist-water}{{9}{16}{SHAP dependence plot for distance to permanent water (Random Forest, 1{,}000 training rows). Points are individual samples coloured by NDWI; the black line and band show the decile-binned median and interquartile range of the SHAP value. The relationship is strongly non-monotonic: samples within the first distance bin (median $\approx 30$~m) receive clearly negative SHAP values, while all farther bins shift toward positive contributions}{figure.caption.14}{}}
